Bridge 0125: keep the final render passes across frames. Every pass instance made its VkRenderPass with
vkCreateRenderPass2 and destroyed it with the command buffer (render_target::create), though the pass depends only on
its shape and load/store operations. Now create() looks the pass up in the device's KeptFinal map, keyed by everything
it is made of (PassShape, color ops, depth/stencil ops, resolve ops, depth/stencil resolve ops, resolving; the device
profile is one per device); a miss makes it and keeps it (cap 256, past it a per-frame pass as before). Kept passes
are destroyed at device teardown like the compatible ones. made_compatible_pass bypasses it (create_now): its callers
(shared_compatible_pass, attachmentless) keep their own. Framebuffers stay per frame.
Logs `SWEET_M2V_PASS_CACHE PC hits H misses M full F kept N at T s` at the first pass and at most every 2 s.
Knob: SWEET_M2V_PASS_CACHE (off unless set and not 0; off = same results and same work as before).

